==Rules==
{{ColosseumRule|Uber Clearance|2}}

==Battleground==
*3 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*1 [[Othom]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*8 [[Mr. Angel]]s spawn after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*1 [[Angelic Beast Rajakong]] spawns as the boss after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Cala Maria]] spawns after 43.33 seconds<sup>1,300f</sup>.
*2 [[Mooth]]s spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
*2 [[Mini White Cyclone]]s spawn after 73.33 seconds<sup>2,200f</sup>, delay 70~73.33 seconds<sup>2,100f~2,200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Brollow]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*3 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 106.67 seconds<sup>3,200f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*1 [[Ancient Magamojoe]] spawns after 126.67 seconds<sup>3,800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Since the threats come out roughly one trait at a time, you can bring specialists who only target one of them, especially Ubers with their decreased cost and cooldown. When the Othom spawns, try to rush it before the other threats come out—[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] will likely be enough. Then, use a standard setup for Rajakong (e.g. [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]]) and also burst him down. The Cyclones are completely hamstrung by [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]], but then the real threat spawns. Magamojoe will certainly require dedicated counters in your lineup, especially certain Legend cats such as [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]] or [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]]. Also, any Surge-immune units can be helpful, though perhaps not necessary if you feel like trying your luck. Once the duck is dead, the stage is won.

